From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:39:51 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 080/230] Make the crash card render, gate the dev token, drop
 the ad switch
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The ErrorBoundary fallback read t(), but the boundary sits OUTSIDE
I18nProvider, so the recovery card itself threw and a render crash became
the white screen the boundary exists to prevent — its copy is hardcoded
English now.

currentAuthToken()'s production guard was compiled to `typeof process`, which
is false in every browser, so production sent the hardcoded `dev:1` bearer
token instead of returning null; it reads import.meta.env.PROD, which Vite
resolves at build time. isTelegram() treated the empty initData string the
SDK leaves outside Telegram as proof of a Telegram client.

ADS_ENABLED gated nothing (both ad units are raw markup in index.html), so
AdBanner.tsx, the vite define and its declaration are gone, and the privacy
copy no longer claims the web build shows no ads.

